# dotenv environment variable files
#
# One env file, `.env`, and it never enters git — it carries working
# credentials. `.env.example` is the committed template that documents every
# key with blank values. Deployments set real environment variables instead of
# shipping a file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# temp directory
.temp
.tmp

# Runtime data
pids
*.pid
*.seed
*.pid.lock

# Diagnostic reports (https://nodejs.org/api/report.html)
report.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.json
